Fowler smell baseline (judgement calls only; documented repo standards override):
- Mysterious Name: name doesn't reveal what it does/holds -> rename.
- Duplicated Code: same logic shape in more than one hunk/file -> extract shared shape.
- Feature Envy: method reaches into another object's data more than its own -> move method.
- Data Clumps: same fields/params travel together -> bundle into a type.
- Primitive Obsession: primitive standing in for a domain concept -> small type.
- Repeated Switches: same switch/if-cascade recurs -> polymorphism or shared map.
- Shotgun Surgery: one logical change forces scattered edits -> gather module.
- Divergent Change: one module edited for unrelated reasons -> split.
- Speculative Generality: abstraction for needs the spec doesn't have -> delete.
- Message Chains: long a.b().c().d() navigation -> hide behind one method.
- Middle Man: class/function mostly delegates -> cut it.
- Refused Bequest: subclass ignores most inherited -> composition.

